{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>Do not harass them, etc.</b> He forbade them only war against Moab, but they would terrorize them and appear to them as though armed; therefore it is written (Numbers 22) ״וַיָּגָר מוֹאָב מִפְּנֵי הָעָם״ — for they would plunder and despoil them. But concerning the children of Ammon it is said (verse 19) ״וְאַל תִּתְגָּר בָם״ — no harassment at all, as reward for their mother's modesty, that she did not publicize her father, as the elder one did who named her son Moab (Bava Kama 38)." "<b>Ar.</b> The name of the province."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:45:40.136495877Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}